<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">help</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">help</ansi> command looks up guidance on a command.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">help say</ansi>
  Find help on the command <ansi fg="command">say</ansi>.

Three kinds of thing show up in the lists below:
  <ansi fg="command">Commands</ansi> are actions you can always take -- move, look, talk, fight.
  <ansi fg="skill">Skills</ansi> are trades and knacks that sharpen the more you use them.
  <ansi fg="spellname">Spells</ansi> are what you channel with <ansi fg="command">cast</ansi> -- type <ansi fg="command">spells</ansi> for the ones you know.

Here are some <ansi fg="skill">skills</ansi> and <ansi fg="command">commands</ansi> to look up to get started:
